1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,313
Why do my stream clips take hours?

2
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:07,137
VOD-first clippers only start after your stream ends.

3
00:00:07,137 --> 00:00:10,332
They download the whole VOD and put it in a queue.

4
00:00:10,332 --> 00:00:17,937
Eklipse's own site says clips typically land 20 to 60 minutes after the stream ends, and longer when the queue is busy.

5
00:00:18,887 --> 00:00:21,755
ClipMe's engine can clip during the stream itself.

6
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:25,884
It captures the stream in windows, so clips land while it's still going.

7
00:00:26,834 --> 00:00:33,170
It ranks every moment with a multi-signal model, and on Kick and Twitch, chat activity is one of the signals.

8
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:36,465
There's no per-minute credit meter.

9
00:00:36,465 --> 00:00:40,285
Starter is free with a watermark, and Pro is $29 a month.

10
00:00:41,235 --> 00:00:45,000
See the best AI clipping tools for Kick at clipme.com.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,952
Paste a VOD and try it free.

